cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "The Attested Bible: a verse-level evidence graph"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
authors:
  - name: "Analytical Solutions"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Analytical-Solutions/attested-bible-data"
url: "https://github.com/Analytical-Solutions/attested-bible-data"
abstract: >-
  A verse-level evidence graph for Matthew, Mark, Luke, John and Acts. Each
  historical claim is linked to archaeological finds, inscriptions, coins,
  manuscripts and ancient writings, with an A-D strength grade, a note and a
  verified verbatim source excerpt. Evidence in tension and searches that found
  nothing are recorded alongside confirmations. AI-assisted research; see
  METHODS.md.
keywords:
  - bible
  - archaeology
  - epigraphy
  - new testament
  - knowledge graph
  - historical evidence
